<title>NETHERLANDS: DSM hydrocarbon margins drag on profits.</title>
<headline>DSM hydrocarbon margins drag on profits.</headline>
<dateline>HEERLEN, Netherlands 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch chemicals group DSM said full-year operating profits had been pressured by lower margins for hydrocarbons and polymers and for the industrial chemicals caprolactam and acrylonitrile.</p>
<p>&quot;The decrease in operating result is due mainly to lower margins (selling prices per tonne less variable costs) for hydrocarbons, polyethylene, polypropylene, caprolactam and acrylonitrile,&quot; DSM said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company earlier reported full-year operating profits slumped to 998 million guilders in 1996 from 1.52 billion guilders in 1995.</p>
